{
  "id": "combination-sum-iii",
  "questionId": "combination-sum-iii",
  "slug": "combination-sum-iii",
  "title": "Combination Sum III",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Backtracking",
  "patterns": [
    "backtracking"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "this is Combinations (choose k of {1..9}) with an extra running-sum constraint bolted on",
    "recurse with (start digit, numbers still needed, sum still needed); try each digit from start to 9",
    "after picking a digit, recurse with start = digit + 1 (each digit used at most once) and both counters decremented accordingly",
    "record the combination when numbers-still-needed hits 0 and sum-still-needed is exactly 0 at the same time - and prune early by stopping a branch as soon as the running sum exceeds n or the remaining digits available (9 - start + 1) can't possibly fill the remaining count"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "checking only the sum condition without also checking the count is exactly k, which can under- or over-count",
    "not pruning when the running sum already exceeds n, wasting time exploring hopeless branches",
    "allowing digits outside 1-9 or reusing a digit within the same combination"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two integers, `k` and `n`.\n\n**Return every combination of `k` distinct numbers, each chosen from 1 to 9, that adds up to `n`.**\n\nEach combination uses each number at most once, and no two combinations in the result contain the same set of numbers.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= k <= 9",
      "1 <= n <= 60",
      "each number from 1 to 9 is used at most once per combination"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "n too small for any valid combination of k distinct digits (answer is empty)",
      "k = 9 (only one possible combination: all digits 1-9, if n matches their sum)",
      "k = 1 (each valid single digit equal to n)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "k = 3, n = 7",
        "output": "[[1, 2, 4]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1, 2, 4]]",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "k = 3, n = 9",
        "output": "[[1, 2, 6], [1, 3, 5], [2, 3, 4]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1, 2, 6], [1, 3, 5], [2, 3, 4]]",
        "explanation": ""
